1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
Short version, if you just got here.

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:07,120
I was three weeks behind on my rental car
when a passenger left two hundred grand in

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,520
my trunk, and I took it to the police.

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:13,680
By then my passenger, Harold, had
been arrested for stealing it,

5
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:16,240
and his daughter, Laura, swore he didn't.

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,480
Then his boss got on speakerphone and
offered me twenty grand to sign a

7
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,960
statement and go home. I signed.

8
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,520
I told myself it wasn't my business.

9
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,360
That the police would figure it out.

10
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:31,800
That twenty thousand dollars was just
the reward for doing the right thing.

11
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,960
Detective Bell slid the
paper over without a word.

12
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,360
Laura didn't look at me when I left.

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,760
She just sat there, staring at the floor,
with her car keys still in her hand.

14
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,760
Brandt's office wired the money on Monday.

15
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:46,080
I caught up on the car.

16
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,600
I paid off the hospital.

17
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:52,200
I wrote "paid in full" across the
bill and stuck it back on the fridge.

18
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:54,880
And for about three weeks, life was good.

19
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,720
I picked up extra shifts.

20
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,560
I slept in on Sundays.

21
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,120
I bought my mom flowers for no reason.

22
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,640
Harold stayed in jail.

23
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,000
I read about it once, and
then I stopped reading.

24
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,680
Then the rental program called.

25
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:12,400
My contract was ending, and
they wanted the car back clean.

26
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:13,720
So on a Sunday,

27
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:18,160
I took it to a self-service car wash and
vacuumed it out for the first time in,

28
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:20,320
honestly, months.

29
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,680
Under the passenger seat,

30
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,840
my hand hit something taped
to the bottom of the frame.

31
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,480
A thick envelope.

32
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:31,080
Inside was a thumb drive and a
note, in shaky ballpoint pen.

33
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,320
"I'm sorry.

34
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,080
You're my plan B.

35
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:38,120
Take this to the federal
investigators, not the local station.

36
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:41,080
Please." It was signed Harold.

37
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,680
"I'm sorry."

38
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:46,560
Same thing he'd said at the airport,
with his hand on my shoulder.

39
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,480
I thought about that red light.

40
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:53,133
The way he leaned forward and reached
under the seat for ten whole seconds.

41
00:01:53,187 --> 00:01:55,360
"Dropped my pen," he'd said.

42
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,400
He never dropped a pen.

43
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,760
I sat in that car wash for an hour.

44
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:04,840
Somebody behind me honked twice,
and I just waved them around.

45
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:09,813
Twenty thousand dollars of Russell
Brandt's money had paid off my whole life.

46
00:02:09,867 --> 00:02:13,000
And Harold had trusted
me, a total stranger,

47
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,480
with the one thing that could get him out.

48
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,920
Not the cash.

49
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,040
This.

50
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:21,840
On Monday morning, I drove to
the federal building downtown.

51
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:25,560
I parked across the street and sat
there with the envelope on my lap,

52
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,200
watching people go in and
out of those glass doors.

53
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:32,160
I checked my phone, like, ten times.

54
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,480
I almost started the car twice.

55
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,880
Signing that paper had been easy.

56
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,907
This was the hard part.

57
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:43,240
And honestly, I still don't know if
that morning was the end of this story,

58
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,760
or the start of a whole different one.

59
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,680
That's ending four of four.

60
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:51,760
If you've seen all four, you
know the whole thing now.

61
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:55,680
The bag, the money, the
thumb drive, all of it.

62
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,280
If you haven't, you're
still missing a piece.

63
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,760
Go back and find it.

64
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,120
The full map is pinned in the comments.
